            <ArticleTitle>Pseudomeningocele nerve root entrapment after lumbar discectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1501-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">A case report of pseudomeningocele with nerve root entrapment after lumbar discectomy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report a rare cause of recurrent sciatica.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A unique case of delayed nerve root entrapment within the neck of an iatrogenic pseudomeningocele is described. The relevant literature is reviewed.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This case illustrates the possible consequences of not repairing a dural tear and reinforces the importance of a careful surgical approach to the lumbar spine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
